From 9df0206cdeeef1ae174d3b0190474755914e4d1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:12:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/28] WIP loader: redefine -lzm auto; gate the managed PLE
 reader OFF

- on = mmap lazy, off = resident, auto = upstream auto
- drop the --lazy-buffer-size CLI arg; the managed LRU PLE reader is now
  opt-in via LLAMA_LAZY_BUF_MB=<MiB> and OFF by default
- measured: managed 1090/1184 vs mmap 1219/1217 vs resident 1285/1232 t/s
  at pp8192/32768 (-b/-ub 8192); the managed reader does unlock the
  parked -b/-ub 16384 context (1118.7 -> 1125.5 t/s)
- test-llama-archs drives the managed budget through the env now
- all lazy modes remain text-identical (7e4a6a4e66fb)
